# Try the KubeShield API from VS Code with the "REST Client" extension
# (humao.rest-client). Click "Send Request" above each ### block, top to bottom.
# Start the server first: Run and Debug -> "API (in-memory store)".
#
# Pick the "local" environment (bottom-right of VS Code) or edit @host below.

@host = http://127.0.0.1:8110
@email = you@example.com
@password = a long passphrase

### Health
GET {{host}}/healthz

### 1. Sign up. Closed by default: only the very first account on a server is accepted.
POST {{host}}/v1/auth/signup
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "display_name": "You",
  "password": "{{password}}",
  "organization_name": "Acme",
  "organization_slug": "acme"
}

### 2. Log in. The token is shown once; later requests pick it up automatically.
# @name login
POST {{host}}/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "password": "{{password}}"
}

###
@token = {{login.response.body.$.token}}

### 3. Who am I, and which organizations am I in?
# @name me
GET {{host}}/v1/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###
@orgId = {{me.response.body.$.organizations[0].id}}

### 4. Register a cluster
# @name cluster
POST {{host}}/v1/organizations/{{orgId}}/clusters
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "kind-local",
  "provider": "kind"
}

###
@clusterId = {{cluster.response.body.$.id}}

### 5. Queue a scan (only recorded as "queued"; nothing runs it until a later phase)
POST {{host}}/v1/organizations/{{orgId}}/clusters/{{clusterId}}/scans
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 6. List the cluster's scans
GET {{host}}/v1/organizations/{{orgId}}/clusters/{{clusterId}}/scans
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 7. Create an agent token (shown once)
# @name agentToken
POST {{host}}/v1/organizations/{{orgId}}/clusters/{{clusterId}}/agent-tokens
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###
@agentSecret = {{agentToken.response.body.$.token}}

### 8. Check the agent token works
GET {{host}}/v1/agent/whoami
Authorization: Bearer {{agentSecret}}

### 9. Members of the organization (owners and admins only)
GET {{host}}/v1/organizations/{{orgId}}/members
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 10. Add someone who already has an account (404 until that person has signed up)
POST {{host}}/v1/organizations/{{orgId}}/members
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "teammate@example.com",
  "role": "member"
}

### 11. What happened? The audit log (owners and admins only)
GET {{host}}/v1/organizations/{{orgId}}/audit-logs
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 12. Log out (revokes this session token)
POST {{host}}/v1/auth/logout
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
